// Note: Text that comes after "//" is ignored, which allows
// you to write notes - like the one you're reading now!

title
  Raider lvl 5-8 (level 2)

  // Raider (lvl 1-4) 
  // Raider Scum (lvl 2-5) 
  // Raider Psycho (lvl 3-6) 
  // Raider Scavver (lvl 4-7) 
  // Raider Waster (lvl 5-8) 
  // Raider Survivalist (lvl 6-9) 
  // Raider Veteran (lvl 7-10) 
  // Raider Boss (lvl 8-11)  

  
                       // general
  // low level raiders with low quality gear. Typically they just wear whatever they can find and rarely have quality armor. 
  // for a boss/elite/leader use a higher level raider table.

  
                      // armor
  // prioritize raider based armor by^x5 more than regular
  // headwear is always random and not worn
  // a single piece of piecemeal is ^3 more likely, a pair of piecemeal ^2 more likely, a full set is normal rate
  // raiders will likely use lower level armor so add^+1 to the lowest level armor on each raider tier


                     // weapons
  // raiders will likely use lower level weapons so add^+1 to the lowest level weapons on each raider tier

  
                     //consumables
  // as with most humans, they drop two consumables with a priority to booze and chems at ^x3


                   //Junk
  // raiders typically dont care too much for junk so they only carry basic stuff
  

output
	After [pack] [Headwear], [Clothing], [Armor], [Guns_and_Ammo], [Melee_Weapon], [Consumable], [Consumable], [Caps], and a [Junk].

  
pack
	searching the body you find

  
